    <h1>Full-Stack Web Development Syllabus</h1>
    <p>Course Code: <strong>CS-101</strong> | Duration: <strong>12 Weeks</strong></p>

    <hr>

    <!-- COURSE METADATA USING A DESCRIPTION LIST -->
    <h2>Course Overview</h2>
    <dl>
        <dt><strong>Prerequisites</strong></dt>
        <dd>Basic computer literacy and familiarity with a code editor (VS Code).</dd>

        <dt><strong>Grading Breakdown</strong></dt>
        <dd>
            <!-- Unordered list nested inside a description definition -->
            <ul>
                <li>Weekly Lab Exercises: 40%</li>
                <li>Midterm Project: 25%</li>
                <li>Final Capstone Application: 35%</li>
            </ul>
        </dd>
    </dl>

    <hr>

    <!-- MAIN SYLLABUS OUTLINE USING NESTED & MIXED LISTS -->
    <h2>Module Breakdown</h2>

    <!-- Top-level Ordered List for sequential modules -->
    <ol>
        <li>
            <strong>Module 1: HTML5 Foundations</strong>
            <!-- Nested Unordered List for topics inside Module 1 -->
            <ul>
                <li>Document Structure &amp; Boilerplate</li>
                <li>Text Formatting &amp; Character Entities</li>
                <li>Lists &amp; Navigation
                    <!-- Deeper nested Ordered List for sub-steps -->
                    <ol type="a">
                        <li>Unordered Lists (<code>&lt;ul&gt;</code>)</li>
                        <li>Ordered Lists (<code>&lt;ol&gt;</code>)</li>
                        <li>Description Lists (<code>&lt;dl&gt;</code>)</li>
                    </ol>
                </li>
                <li>Semantic HTML5 Elements</li>
            </ul>
        </li>

        <li>
            <strong>Module 2: CSS3 &amp; Responsive Design</strong>
            <ul>
                <li>Selectors, Specificity &amp; Box Model</li>
                <li>Layout Systems
                    <ul>
                        <li>Flexbox for 1D Layouts</li>
                        <li>CSS Grid for 2D Layouts</li>
                    </ul>
                </li>
                <li>Media Queries &amp; Mobile-First Design</li>
            </ul>
        </li>

        <li>
            <strong>Module 3: JavaScript &amp; DOM Manipulation</strong>
            <ul>
                <li>Variables, Data Types &amp; Functions</li>
                <li>DOM Selection &amp; Event Listeners</li>
                <li>Fetching Data from APIs
                    <ol type="i">
                        <li>Understanding JSON</li>
                        <li>Promises &amp; <code>async/await</code></li>
                    </ol>
                </li>
            </ul>
        </li>
    </ol>

